flowchart LR
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: after a transaction is recorded, in which reports does it appear, who receives each report, and what are the deadlines?
  %% READING: left = reports of one national agency. Middle = the system or channel. Right = the receiver and what the receiver produces from it.
  %% SOURCES: the list of BFARs, their contents, deadlines, receivers and the rule that only URS-generated copies are accepted [JC2019-1]. Deadlines restated for FY 2026 [NBC599]. Reports through URS until agencies migrate to BTMS [GAA2026-GP]. Year-end trial balances and statements by 14 February, COA annual report by 30 September [PD1445 s.41]. AFR System for submission of statements to COA [COA-GAS]. COA annual report to the President and Congress [CONST IX-D.4]. Cash Operations Report of BTr [NBC599]. Corporations: statements by 14 February [COA2015-004]. Local governments: eSRE [eSRE].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: quarterly financial statements to the auditor, the agency audit report as a separate document for each agency, the fiscal reports that DBM and DOF publish, publication on agency websites.

  subgraph AG["ONE NATIONAL AGENCY PREPARES"]
    A1["BAR 1  Quarterly Physical Report of Operations<br/>actual outputs against the physical plan<br/>within 30 days after each quarter"]
    A2["FAR 1, 1-A, 1-B, 1-C  Appropriations, allotments,<br/>obligations, disbursements and balances.<br/>By program, by object, list of allotments,<br/>inter-agency transfers. Within 30 days after each quarter"]
    A3["FAR 2, 2-A and FAR 6  Budget, utilization and<br/>disbursements of off-budget funds and trust receipts<br/>within 30 days after each quarter"]
    A4["FAR 3  Aging of due and demandable obligations<br/>within 30 days after the end of the year"]
    A5["FAR 4  Monthly Report of Disbursements<br/>by type of disbursement authority<br/>by the 10th day of the next month"]
    A6["FAR 5  Quarterly Report of Revenue and Other Receipts<br/>within 30 days after each quarter"]
    A7["Trial balances and financial statements<br/>year-end set by 14 February"]
    A8["Paid vouchers, journal entry vouchers<br/>and supporting documents"]
  end

  URS["URS<br/>Unified Reporting System (DBM)<br/>Only reports generated by URS,<br/>signed, are accepted"]:::sys
  AFRS["AFR System (COA)<br/>online submission of<br/>financial statements"]:::sys
  AUD["Direct submission to the<br/>COA audit team<br/>assigned to the agency"]:::sys

  subgraph RC["RECEIVERS AND WHAT THEY PRODUCE"]
    R1["DBM<br/>monitors spending and performance,<br/>adjusts later releases of cash authority,<br/>uses actual figures in the next budget documents"]
    R2["BTr<br/>receives FAR 3, FAR 4 and FAR 5,<br/>manages cash, publishes the monthly<br/>Cash Operations Report"]
    R4["COA audit team<br/>examines transactions and statements,<br/>issues the audit report of the agency"]
    R3["COA Government Accountancy Sector<br/>consolidates statements into the<br/>Annual Financial Report, by 30 September"]
  end

  R5["President and Congress<br/>receive the COA annual report.<br/>Congress uses reports in budget hearings"]

  A1 --> URS
  A2 --> URS
  A3 --> URS
  A4 --> URS
  A5 --> URS
  A6 --> URS
  A7 --> AFRS
  A8 --> AUD
  URS --> R1
  URS --> R2
  URS --> R4
  AUD --> R4
  AFRS --> R3
  R3 --> R5
  R4 --> R5

  OTH["OTHER SPENDING BODIES REPORT SEPARATELY<br/>Government corporations: statements to COA by 14 February,<br/>quarterly reports through URS.<br/>Local governments: statements of receipts and<br/>expenditures to BLGF through eSRE"]
  R5 ~~~ OTH

